# Path to the Slay the Spire 2 install (the folder that contains data_sts2_windows_x86_64).
# Windows paths such as C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Slay the Spire 2 are accepted.
STS2_INSTALL_DIR=

# Optional. Folder that contains RitsuLib.References.props.
# Leave empty to search:
#   $STS2_INSTALL_DIR/mods/STS2-RitsuLib/
#   $STS2_INSTALL_DIR/mods/RitsuLib/
#   the Steam Workshop download for item 3747602295
# Point this at a GitHub extract or the Workshop download if the bundle lives elsewhere.
RITSULIB_DIR=

# Optional. To compile against a different RitsuLib variant, pass -p:RitsuLibReferenceTarget=<x.y.z>.
# The value must name an exact folder under RitsuLib/compat (this bundle ships 0.107.1,
# 0.111.0 and 0.113.0). The default is 0.111.0, which matches the oldest game build this mod
# supports.
# Note this is the compile reference only; the runtime requirement lives in the manifests
# as min_game_version.

# Optional. Game install to compile against, when it differs from STS2_INSTALL_DIR.
# One BetterRewards.dll serves both the public branch and public-beta, so it must always be
# compiled against the OLDEST supported build; newer APIs are reached by reflection from
# src/Core/Sts2ApiCompat.cs. Keeping a pinned 0.111.x snapshot here means switching your Steam
# install to public-beta cannot leak 0.113-only members into the build.
#
# A snapshot at .reference/<min_game_version>/ (containing
# data_sts2_windows_x86_64/sts2.dll, GodotSharp.dll and 0Harmony.dll) is picked up
# automatically, so plain `dotnet build` is protected too -- that path does not read .env.
# Set this only when the snapshot lives somewhere else. The folder is gitignored: those are
# copyrighted game files and must not be redistributed.
# Leave empty to fall back to the .reference snapshot, then to STS2_INSTALL_DIR.
STS2_REFERENCE_DIR=
